---
description: Agentic loop Definition of Done, verify-first, revert over iterate
alwaysApply: true
---

# Agentic loop (Observe -> Act -> Verify -> Decide -> Repeat)

Applies when implementing or fixing code. Read project AGENTS.md for repo-specific verify commands.

## Definition of Done - task is done when ALL are true

1. Acceptance criteria from plan/task/AGENTS.md are met (cite which).
2. Verification command exits 0 (name the exact command run).
3. No new linter/type errors in touched files.
4. Shrimp verify_task score >=80 OR verifier pass OR explicit user sign-off.

Even C0 fix tasks require a one-line verify (lint or targeted test) before marking done.

## Verify-first

Before first edit: state verify command(s) from AGENTS.md or scripts/quality-gate.py.

After changes: run verify; if FAIL, fix and re-run (max 5 iterations, then STOP and report blocker).

## Revert over iterate

If the agent diverges from an approved plan: revert, refine plan, re-run - do not patch via many follow-up prompts.

## Stop conditions

- 3 identical verify failures or no file diff after 2 fix attempts -> STOP + blocker report.
- Destructive ops: rollback plan + user confirmation first.
- Shrimp continuous mode: stop on verify <80, ambiguity, or out-of-scope blocker.

## Model selection

- Plan / architecture / security review -> thinking model.
- Implement / fix / run tests -> fast model.
